rm-limited and off the ballot. Republican Ty Masterson faces Democrat Cindy Holscher, and polling since mid-September has settled into a modest Republican lead. The largest recent surveys, from YouGov and the New York Times/Siena, show Masterson up three and five points, and reporting indicates independent voters are fueling his edge.\n\nThe race is not closed, though. A favorable national climate for Democrats has produced competitive governor's races in red-leaning states, and one Democratic-sponsored September poll briefly showed Holscher ahead. Most ratings call the race Lean R, and prediction markets put Holscher's chances between roughly a quarter and two-in-five. The fight over AI data centers has roiled Kansas politics and may define the campaign's final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1817, "margin": -4.47}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.161, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1643, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1648, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1797, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1739, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.215, "margin": -4.3}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2315, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2051, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2039, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2527, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2551, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2356, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1928, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1955, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2198, "margin": -3.8}]}